  "title": "I-CARE: International Cardiac Arrest REsearch consortium EEG Database (BIDS)",
  "description": "The I-CARE database contains continuous EEG and, where available, ECG recordings with baseline clinical information from comatose adult patients after cardiac arrest, collected at academic hospitals in the United States, the Netherlands and Belgium. This BIDS conversion of PhysioNet release 2.1 covers 607 patients and about 32,700 hours of hourly recordings. Outcome is given as the dichotomised Cerebral Performance Category. The data support neurological prognostication research and were the training set of the George B. Moody PhysioNet Challenge 2023.",
  "methods_description": "Continuous EEG with standard 10-20 channels (19-21 per recording) plus ECG and reference channels was recorded in ICU patients, at native sampling rates of 200-2048 Hz depending on site. WFDB records were merged per hourly segment into EDF files without numerical loss. Channel units were inferred to be microvolts.",
